[E0348] Error: `?` on `Option<i64>` needs the lambda to answer one too
    ╭─[ err/449_propagation_in_lambdas/main.wip:16:11 ]
    │
 16 │         val h = half(n)?
    │                 ────┬───
    │                     ╰───── returns from the lambda
 17 │         return h + 1
    │                ──┬──
    │                  ╰──── this lambda answers `i64`
    │
    │ Help: `?` leaves the lambda, not the function around it: for every value or none, collect them with `Option::collect(values.forwards().map(…))` and write the `?` after it
    │
    │ Note: `?` on an `Option` returns `.None`, so the lambda must answer an `Option`
────╯
[E0348] Error: `?` on `Result<i64, str>` needs the lambda to answer one too
